  "title": "Alawieh2025: Motor-imagery BCI dataset with transcutaneous spinal stimulation",
  "description": "A longitudinal EEG dataset of two-class (left/right hand) motor imagery brain-computer interface training combined with transcutaneous electrical spinal cord stimulation. It includes 27 participants, 25 able-bodied and 2 with spinal cord injury. Recordings use 32 EEG channels and 3 EOG channels at 512 Hz, and the data are distributed in a MOABB-compatible BIDS format.",
  "methods_description": "EEG was recorded with an ANT Neuro eego amplifier and Ag/AgCl electrodes at 512 Hz (32 EEG and 3 EOG channels, 10-20 montage, reference CPz, ground AFz). Participants performed cue-based, offline kinesthetic motor imagery of left or right hand movement in 4 s trials.",
